@copilot Update this PR directly to simplify its regression tests. The user wants to keep the production fix as-is and integrate the regression assertions into the existing matcher test instead of adding new test methods.

In instrumentation-docs/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/docs/utils/FileManagerTest.java, remove the newly added testIsValidInstrumentationPathExcludesSourceDirectories() and testGetInstrumentationPathsExcludesSourceDirectories() methods. In the existing testIsValidInstrumentationPath(), add two direct assertions that isValidInstrumentationPath() returns false for the actual offending path instrumentation/spring/spring-integration-4.1/library/src/version41Test/java/io/opentelemetry/javaagent, once with forward slashes and once with Windows backslashes. Use the two literal paths directly in the assertions. No source-set matrix, new filesystem fixture, new test method, or helper is needed. Preserve all pre-existing tests.

Keep the production FileManager.java change exactly unchanged, including the /src/ regex exclusion. Do not refactor discovery or introduce metadata-based registration. Run the narrowest relevant formatting followed by the FileManagerTest unit tests. Acceptance: the PR's only new test coverage is those two false assertions in the existing matcher test, with the one-line production fix retained.
